{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver","id":451626,"title":"Spirits of Silver","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T09:57:53-07:00","id":451626,"title":"Spirits of Silver","content":"Is there any official setting info about werewolves' (both Forsaken and Pure) relationship with spirits of metallic silver. <br /> <br /> If not, have such spirits interacted with werewolves in your game, and how did you handle it. Were such spirits deadly and wisely avoided, highly sought after and supplicated for powerful fetishes and rites, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T11:16:48-07:00","id":451796,"title":"","content":"There's definitely no official info for 2e. I really like the idea though. I'd expect every DM to handle it differently.<br /> <br /> Would all attacks from manifested or Claimed be considered silver?<br /> As for harnessing them, it'd be like trying to befriend a nuclear waste spirit. Hard to give it what it wants! :-D<br /> I wonder if they're natural enemies of Lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T12:07:27-07:00","id":451875,"title":"","content":"Page 121 of Blasphemies mentions a bit:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Asah Gadar seek to use silver-spirits against the Forsaken; powerful silver-spirits have been known to manifest Numen-like powers over their material in the physical realm and threaten werewolves with unexpected, eerie silver-based assaults.<br /> <br /> However, these spirits require a great deal of chiminage first and are reluctant to strike Luna\u2019s children without good reason. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T12:24:33-07:00","id":451912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=451796#post451796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they're natural enemies of Lunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess it would be quite the opposite. Luna could curse the Uratha with a weakness against silver, because silver is somewhat related to her portfolio (just as gold is for Helios). Even if the silver spirits do not answer to Luna in a hierarchical sense, she could poblably make them answer for their deeds. This could be why in Satchel's quote silver spirits are reluctant to strike Luna's children without good reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:29:59-07:00","id":452164,"title":"","content":"While pondering non-traditional notions of silver, I also began to wonder about the effects on werewolves of perfected silver,<i>Lunargent</i>, from Mage. particularly since DaveB stated that perfected metals will receive greater treatment in Mage 2e and he was one of the writers for WtF 2e.<br /> <br /> Would it have the same effect on werewolves as mundane silver, no effect at all, possess unique or unpredictable properties, or would its presence to both Forsaken and Pure be akin to carrying around a radiological or biological WMD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typos 03-22-2015, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:32:12-07:00","id":452167,"title":"","content":"I think it would probably have the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T17:54:57-07:00","id":452187,"title":"","content":"I'd treat Lunargent as I'd treat W:tA moonsilver \u2014 it is INCREDIBLY potent and not to be messed with lightly. In W:tA, you had to travel to the Shadow of the Moon and do a quest for one of Luna's avatars to get it, and it did double the damage regular silver did to werewolves. In W:tF 2e, I would think that Urdaga get 2x the injury from it, and the Anshega get a staggering 4x damage because it's silver in its strongest form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:52:17-07:00","id":452448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=451875#post451875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 121 of Blasphemies mentions a bit:</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a certain amount of sense. I imagine most Silver Spirits don't want to be on the receiving end of an Apocalypse style genocide against them.<br /> If they are sapient enough to realize it, they would be understandably wary of getting involved in Werewolf politics. It rarely goes well for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T03:50:08-07:00","id":452477,"title":"","content":"Hardcore idea: A pack of Blood Talons taking a silver spirit as their totem, so as to better hunt the Most Worthy Prey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:18:59-07:00","id":452490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=452477#post452477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardcore idea: A pack of Blood Talons taking a silver spirit as their totem, so as to better hunt the Most Worthy Prey</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems like a serious violation of the Oath of the Moon just waiting to explode against the pack, as well as a massive implied threat against even otherwise allied Forsaken. Moreover, what remotely sane (at least for a spirit) silver spirit would agree to be a totem. The potential pack ban would also likely be most &quot;unpleasant.&quot; I would think that silver spirits would be in the same category as Lunes and Helions as really bad totem ideas except for packs with a death wish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> However, if we're discussing WMD-level totems, I would go for the full monty and seek a Lunargent Spirit. I would imagine that nothing would say &quot;bad ass Uratha&quot; like a totem of perfected silver.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:12:04-07:00","id":452813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=452490#post452490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That seems like a serious violation of the Oath of the Moon just waiting to explode against the pack, as well as a massive implied threat against even otherwise allied Forsaken. Moreover, what remotely sane (at least for a spirit) silver spirit would agree to be a totem. The potential pack ban would also likely be most &quot;unpleasant.&quot; I would think that silver spirits would be in the same category as Lunes and Helions as really bad totem ideas except for packs with a death wish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, if we're discussing WMD-level totems, I would go for the full monty and seek a Lunargent Spirit. I would imagine that nothing would say &quot;bad ass Uratha&quot; like a totem of perfected silver.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said hardcore. I'm imagining the Werewolf equivalent of <i>The Lost Boys</i> - asshole young Uratha who think they can live fast, die young and leave a beautiful corpse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:12:52-07:00","id":452868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=452813#post452813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said hardcore. I'm imagining the Werewolf equivalent of <i>The Lost Boys</i> - asshole young Uratha who think they can live fast, die young and leave a beautiful corpse</div> </div> </div> </div> Alternatively, a young, isolated(maybe live near a silver mine?) pack of Ghost Wolves who have no idea what they're getting into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:06:38-07:00","id":452975,"title":"","content":"Since the vulnerability to silver is an aspect of Luna's punishment for the Uratha, it would seem weird to me if she made a super version of it that could wipe out the entire race and make it available to anyone but herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:12:48-07:00","id":452987,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: Have it do what <i>nobody</i> expects it to. Maybe the whole curse thing is a complete myth and the reason werewolves take aggravated is because their body is trying to harmonise with the regular silver and failing because it's not pure enough. Lunargent synchronises properly and well... who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:23:32-07:00","id":453010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=452987#post452987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea: Have it do what <i>nobody</i> expects it to. Maybe the whole curse thing is a complete myth and the reason werewolves take aggravated is because their body is trying to harmonise with the regular silver and failing because it's not pure enough. Lunargent synchronises properly and well... who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe they are just allergic to silver. No curse, just a really averse reaction. Besides, other shapeshifters suffer from the vulnerability too and they have nothing to do with Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:32:32-07:00","id":453015,"title":"","content":"<i>Or do they? </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T12:34:57-07:00","id":453016,"title":"","content":"Luna is the goddess of change, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:02:47-07:00","id":453060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453016#post453016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna is the goddess of change, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I wanted to say. Technically all the shapeshifters fall under Luna's purview at least for a little bit.<br /> <br /> And even then, not all shapeshifters are hurt by silver. I think there is at least one in War Against the Pure that isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:05:09-07:00","id":453064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453060#post453060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly what I wanted to say. Technically all the shapeshifters fall under Luna's purview at least for a little bit.<br /> <br /> And even then, not all shapeshifters are hurt by silver. I think there is at least one in War Against the Pure that isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Midianites, unfortunately, are only mentioned in passing and don't have a full writeup. Whatever they may be, iron and fire are their particular banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:48:48-07:00","id":453355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=452975#post452975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the vulnerability to silver is an aspect of Luna's punishment for the Uratha, it would seem weird to me if she made a super version of it that could wipe out the entire race and make it available to anyone but herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfected Silver, at least as indicated in the various nWOD books, does not occur naturally in the physical world, is not provided by Luna and her lunes, and is VERY rare. Thus far, it's entirely a mage creation, and with all thing mage-y, you never know how their experiments will muck-up the whole universe. In fact, Luna might be quite annoyed that Lunargent was created at all and is formulating an appropriate response, just doing so in a time-frame and reference of a Rank 8 celestial spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe they are just allergic to silver. No curse, just a really averse reaction. Besides, other shapeshifters suffer from the vulnerability too and they have nothing to do with Luna. </div> </div> </div>Do we have confirmation that other shapeshifters similar to uratha still exist in the second edition?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:53:48-07:00","id":453358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453060#post453060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly what I wanted to say. Technically all the shapeshifters fall under Luna's purview at least for a little bit.<br /> <br /> And even then, not all shapeshifters are hurt by silver. I think there is at least one in War Against the Pure that isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I recall correctly (and I certainly my be confusing my WtA with WtF mythologies), I thought some of the other more obscure shapeshifters were vulnerable to gold and iron, rather than silver. Of course, those ever annoying mages have also created perfected gold (Oricalcum) and perfected iron (Siderite) . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:54:57-07:00","id":453361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453355#post453355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have confirmation that other shapeshifters similar to uratha still exist in the second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had confirmation of two new types of Host plus the eminently creepier resurgence of the Halaku in Tokyo alone, plus an instance of probable Machine-influence that's centuries old in Wroclaw and the direct involvement of Destroyer Wolf in Basra, and the relevant chapter of War Against the Pure was very much about Weird Shit In The World Of Darkness; I can think of literally no good reason why their existence would be on the list of Things Removed In Two-Ee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:01:39-07:00","id":453366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perfected Silver, at least as indicated in the various nWOD books, does not occur naturally in the physical world, is not provided by Luna and her lunes, and is VERY rare. Thus far, it's entirely a mage creation, and with all thing mage-y, you never know how their experiments will muck-up the whole universe. In fact, Luna might be quite annoyed that Lunargent was created at all and is formulating an appropriate response, just doing so in a time-frame and reference of a Rank 8 celestial spirit </div> </div> </div>Given the proccess by wich silver becomes lunargent, it is trivially easy for almost any spirit to do it, ditto for Luna themself. It could also occur naturally at a Locus, who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:13:18-07:00","id":453404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453366#post453366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the proccess by wich silver becomes lunargent, it is trivially easy for almost any spirit to do it, ditto for Luna themself. It could also occur naturally at a Locus, who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In addition to not yet knowing the perfected metal rules in MtAw 2e, we've no indication of any Lunargent created by anyone other than mages in exceedingly small quantities, although your proposition is certainly plausible under existing nWOD canon.<br /> <br /> In fact, I could easily imagine the crazed desire and attempt by a powerful silver spirit to continually cross the physical world and Hisil in order to &quot;perfect&quot; itself after watching the strange workings of local mages. Such a spirit could pose a serious risk to uratha, and might be an interesting idea for a chronicle, or at least a very dangerous Siskur-Dah against both the silver spirit as well as the careless mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:23:40-07:00","id":453418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453361#post453361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've had confirmation of two new types of Host plus the eminently creepier resurgence of the Halaku in Tokyo alone, plus an instance of probable Machine-influence that's centuries old in Wroclaw and the direct involvement of Destroyer Wolf in Basra, and the relevant chapter of War Against the Pure was very much about Weird Shit In The World Of Darkness; I can think of literally no good reason why their existence would be on the list of Things Removed In Two-Ee.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> New and unusual Hosts and other miscellaneous oddities in the WOD who have the ability to change their form are not necessarily analogous to either uratha or similar mythological changing breeds. <br /> <br /> Although I have no idea if the changing breeds will be reintroduced in WtF 2e, and am fairly agnostic on the topic, I don't recall any developer or author offering a substantive opinion on the matter. Nevertheless, I can certainly think of a few reasons <i>not</i> to include them, including the diminishment of the uniqueness of uratha in the WOD cosmology and avoiding the ever increasing glut of supernatural creatures in nWOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:51:40-07:00","id":453454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453418#post453418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New and unusual Hosts and other miscellaneous oddities in the WOD who have the ability to change their form are not necessarily analogous to either uratha or similar mythological changing breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shapeshifters being discussed, however, are unified in their mechanical weakness to silver and possession of some variety of rage mechanic, and share space with isolated communities like the town that all wound up turning into mastiffs after a visit from &quot;the Devil&quot; or the recurring clutches of bird-men who live in high places.<br /> <br /> &quot;The changing breeds&quot; have fuckall to do with it. A global community of werewolves does not have its narrative niche threatened by the existence of pockets of strangeness in a world filled with pockets of strangeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:00:45-07:00","id":453468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453454#post453454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shapeshifters being discussed, however, are unified in their mechanical weakness to silver and possession of some variety of rage mechanic, and share space with isolated communities like the town that all wound up turning into mastiffs after a visit from &quot;the Devil&quot; or the recurring clutches of bird-men who live in high places.<br /> <br /> &quot;The changing breeds&quot; have fuckall to do with it. A global community of werewolves does not have its narrative niche threatened by the existence of pockets of strangeness in a world filled with pockets of strangeness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're arguing that shapeshifters analogous or related in some way to uratha (or at least their cosmology) should officially be part of the nWOD. That's fine. However, I was only noting that I've not read anything from anyone from OPP to indicate whether such beings will or will not be included in nWOD 2e, I personally have no strong opinions either way, and that arguments can definitely be made that they should in fact not be included. Of course, even if OPP decides that they will not officially be included, you and others are certainly free to populate your WOD with whoever and whatever you desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:10:45-07:00","id":453472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453468#post453468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're arguing that shapeshifters analogous or related in some way to uratha (or at least their cosmology) should officially be part of the nWOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about Chapter 4 of <i>War Against The Pure</i>, dude. Things like the Brineborn and the Unclean, which have no established mythological relation to the Uratha and are by no means isolated examples of Weird WoD Shit producing creatures with mechanical similarity to the Uratha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, even if OPP decides that they will not officially be included, you and others are certainly free to populate your WOD with whoever and whatever you desire. </div> </div> </div>I literally could not care less about &quot;should&quot; in this discussion and your decision to put words in my mouth does not foster any degree of respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:21:51-07:00","id":453508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453472#post453472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about Chapter 4 of <i>War Against The Pure</i>, dude. Things like the Brineborn and the Unclean, which have no established mythological relation to the Uratha and are by no means isolated examples of Weird WoD Shit producing creatures with mechanical similarity to the Uratha.<br /> <br /> I literally could not care less about &quot;should&quot; in this discussion and your decision to put words in my mouth does not foster any degree of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do not understand your belligerence. This minor issue (ancillary to the thread itself) is whether other major races of shapeshifters with similar mechanics and/or cosmology to uratha will be included in the nWOD 2e. It is my understanding that no one at OPP has yet offered a definitive answer to that question. Whether a WtF 1e book such as War Against the Pure included such beings offers no dispositive indication of what will ultimately be part of the official WtF 2e canon, nor does the fact that &quot;weird shit&quot; already exists in the nWOD. It appears that you are simply offended or angered that I do not share your viewpoint that such beings <i>must </i>be included in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-22-2015, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:43:04-07:00","id":453519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453508#post453508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears that you are simply offended or angered that I do not share your viewpoint that such beings <i>must </i>be included in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing &quot;should&quot; to &quot;must&quot; in your misunderstanding does not make me less annoyed at your mischaracterization, nor does your failure to understand that repeatedly attributing a viewpoint not my own to me is going to try my patience.<br /> <br /> So far things that have been removed in 2e have been fairly explicit or at least directly implicit \u2014 Ghost Children aren't a thing anymore thanks to the changes in the particulars of &quot;The Uratha Shall Cleave To The Human&quot; and how wolf-blooded work, Renown is no longer capped by primary and has condensed the honorary Rank table, instances of spirits and ghosts interacting without a mechanical ability to do so are getting cleaned up thanks to the new Ephemeral Beings rules \u2014 and &quot;other shapeshifters exist&quot; is not one of those adjustments.<br /> <br /> The mythology of the Uratha is irrelevant to the existence or nonexistence of a given supernatural gribbly \u2014 they're stories, and stories that have explicitly gotten things wrong or stopped containing useful information on multiple occasions over time, to boot. Other shapeshifters were textually possible in 1e. 2e brings nothing to the table that negates that possibility and if anything is likely to do the opposite if it does anything at all with it by dint of a generally increased emphasis on the weird.<br /> <br /> It is a diminutive view to take to read this as &quot;Satchel's mad that I disagree with him.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:12:31-07:00","id":453617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453519#post453519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other shapeshifters were textually possible in 1e. 2e brings nothing to the table that negates that possibility and if anything is likely to do the opposite if it does anything at all with it by dint of a generally increased emphasis on the weird.<br /> <br /> It is a diminutive view to take to read this as &quot;Satchel's mad that I disagree with him.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, you're the one who's doing the mischaracterizing. I certainly never stated that anything in 2e &quot;negates the possibility&quot; that the shapeshifters with similar mechanics or cosmology to uratha can appear in 2e. Reread my original inquiry and comments. I simply questioned whether anyone from OPP has actually indicated if such beings will in fact ultimately appear in 2e canon, not whether their appearance could be good, necessary, prudent, consistent with 1e ,or anything else. In fact, as I've stated repeatedly, I don't have a strong opinion either way as I've rarely used them, but readily acknowledge there are legitimate reasons for OPP to both officially include or exclude them in future published books.<br /> <br /> I read you comments as practically insisting that these beings already exist in the nWOD 2e, or at least should or must be included due to 1e references, the inclusion of other oddities in 2e, or just your own personal preference. OPP may ultimately include these types of shapeshifters in 2e, but thus far you've not cited any comments by OPP authors or developers to actually confirm the inclusion of these beings in the official nWOD 2e.<br /> <br /> Again, to the extent it needs to be repeated, everyone can include or exclude what and whom they wish in their own games.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if necessary, I would be happy to continue this discussion in another thread. However, since the issue of other shapeshifters in published 2e books has little, if anything, to do with werewolves' interaction with silver spirits and similar matters, as proffered in my OP, I do not see the wisdom of continuing this issue in this thread, and would have no objection if any mod wished to move or edit this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:21:28-07:00","id":453623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453617#post453617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but thus far you've not cited any comments by OPP authors or developers to actually confirm the inclusion of these beings in the official nWOD 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the God Machine Chronicles it explains that the new rules systems are made to update the storyteller system with what they've learned about gaming and what players want from it. Not that this is restarting the new World of Darkness from scratch. Outside of unihar and merits, nothing really seems to have been taken away.<br /> <br /> But the existence or nonexistence of shapeshifters seems like a derailment in regards to spirits of silver. And of course the super silver metal won't have any special rules until well after Mage second edition is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-22-2015, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:43:04-07:00","id":453698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453623#post453623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the God Machine Chronicles it explains that the new rules systems are made to update the storyteller system with what they've learned about gaming and what players want from it. Not that this is restarting the new World of Darkness from scratch. Outside of unihar and merits, nothing really seems to have been taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your comment is entirely consistent with my point. I'm certainly not stating that the indicated shapeshifters have been or should definitely be removed in 2e, only that I do not recall reading any comments by OPP personnel about them in the new editions. That is why I was so surprised by tenor of the discussion.<br /> <br /> I would note that there have been significant changes in both WtF 2e and the nWOD overall, including, as you mention, the removal of the unihar which fundamentally and drastically altered werewolf interpersonal relations from 1e. Do not also forget other massive shifts in the WtF setting like the inclusion of wolf-blooded and normal humans in packs. WtF 2e is definitely more than some simple crunch patchwork over 1e. Mage and Changeling 2e appear to also be undergoing major setting updates or changes. As to what might officially be included in the entire nWOD 2e in the future, your guess is as good as mine. The issue certainly is not limited to WtF. For instance, similar questions could be directed to VtR 2e, and if and when we might see new versions of Belial's Brood, VII, or any of the innumerable bloodlines, both as to setting and mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-22-2015, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:53:19-07:00","id":454509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=453418#post453418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> New and unusual Hosts and other miscellaneous oddities in the WOD who have the ability to change their form are not necessarily analogous to either uratha or similar mythological changing breeds.<br /> <br /> Although I have no idea if the changing breeds will be reintroduced in WtF 2e, and am fairly agnostic on the topic, I don't recall any developer or author offering a substantive opinion on the matter. Nevertheless, I can certainly think of a few reasons <i>not</i> to include them, including the diminishment of the uniqueness of uratha in the WOD cosmology and avoiding the ever increasing glut of supernatural creatures in nWOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Skinchangers are a thing in Second Edition (See the upcoming relevant chapters in Dark Eras) I can see no reason others would not exist as they have in 1st Edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:05:55-07:00","id":454526,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras is sort of between editions, so far it's written for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:19:12-07:00","id":454549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=454509#post454509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since Skinchangers are a thing in Second Edition (See the upcoming relevant chapters in Dark Eras) I can see no reason others would not exist as they have in 1st Edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would partially agree, and would readily concede that we hardly need even look to the anticipated Dark Eras to easily conclude that other shapeshifters exist in the nWOD. Heck, a great number of mages and vampires easily change forms and could satisfy various horror myths of shapechangers, including of men who change into wolves.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether the nWOD will officially include shapeshifters similiar, mechanically and thematically (e.g., vulnerability to silver, homage to celestine like entities, etc.), to the uratha of WtF 2e, most readily, but not exclusively, recognized by the various changing breeds of the old edition. There was no mention of these beings in WtF 2e or GMC, nor to my knowledge, has OPP indicated the status of their 2e existence.<br /> <br /> I simply noted our lack of current information, and that reasonable arguments exists across the spectrum on whether such particular types of beings (not any or all shapeshifters) should be officially included in nWOD 2e books. I really do not understand how this is in any way controversial, other than for some to believe I'm somehow erroneously challenging their own group's individualized WOD, which can and should include whatever and whomever they want, or that my somewhat clinical analysis might discourage OPP from providing 2e equivalents of these favored characters, which I've certainly not done.<br /> <br /> I would love nothing more than a comment from a OPP developer indicating the status of these types of shapeshifters in 2e in order to lay the discussion to rest, and return to the discussion of silver spirits, perfected silver, and other related matters concerning more esoteric issues concerning werewolves and silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:10:26-07:00","id":454701,"title":"","content":"On that note, is a formless idigam turning into a tidal wave of molten silver a potential danger one faces when fighting one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:19:15-07:00","id":454710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451626-spirits-of-silver?p=454701#post454701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, is a formless idigam turning into a tidal wave of molten silver a potential danger one faces when fighting one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a tidal wave of molten metal is most certainly crazy dangerous! If the molten metal is silver, it would probably just be overkill. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Creating idigam with connections to silver, however, is definitely prospect that should be disturbing to all uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}